1
00:00:00,480 --> 00:00:02,250
Had to or got to?

2
00:00:02,248 --> 00:00:03,418
(Dave:)Sorry.

3
00:00:03,416 --> 00:00:05,916
(Amy:)My fault. I brought him up.
Yeah.

4
00:00:05,919 --> 00:00:07,249
(Dave:)Well, let's change the subject.

5
00:00:07,253 --> 00:00:09,223
(Dave:)No more mentions
of you-know-who.

6
00:00:09,222 --> 00:00:10,952
(laughs)
That's a cool train.

7
00:00:10,957 --> 00:00:13,127
(Dave:)Where did you get that?

8
00:00:14,227 --> 00:00:17,127
♪ Bah, bah, bum-bum,
bah, bum, bum. ♪

9
00:00:18,965 --> 00:00:21,635
(humming tune)

10
00:00:23,570 --> 00:00:27,340
(gargling song)

11
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:28,870
(Sheldon(singing):)This song

12
00:00:28,875 --> 00:00:30,075
(Sheldon:)is never going to stop.

13
00:00:30,076 --> 00:00:31,606
(Sheldon:)Have you ever dealt
with something

14
00:00:31,611 --> 00:00:34,211
(Sheldon:)so relentlessly irritating?

15
00:00:35,081 --> 00:00:38,651
(Leonard:)That's a trick
question, right?

16
00:00:38,651 --> 00:00:40,181
(Sheldon:)Well, I shouldn't
be surprised.

17
00:00:40,186 --> 00:00:41,686
(Sheldon:)There's a rich history of

18
00:00:41,688 --> 00:00:43,358
(Sheldon:)brilliant minds
descending into madness.

19
00:00:43,356 --> 00:00:44,856
PENNY:
Come on, Sheldon.

20
00:00:44,857 --> 00:00:47,557
(Penny:)There are plenty of smart people
who don't have mental problems.

21
00:00:47,560 --> 00:00:48,690
(Leonard:)Yup, she's right.

22
00:00:48,695 --> 00:00:50,665
(Leonard:)For every Newton who had
a psychological issue,

23
00:00:50,663 --> 00:00:52,563
(Leonard:)there's an Edison
who was just a jerk.

24
00:00:52,565 --> 00:00:54,965
(Leonard:)That could
totally be you.

25
00:00:54,968 --> 00:00:58,838
(Sheldon:)Empedocles thought he was a god
and jumped into a volcano.

